# Plan workflow

This rule owns what discovery, planning and Build share: stage boundaries, delegation, the domain map,
the plan folder layout and the user-flow handoffs. Discovery runs whether or not a plan follows; planning
and Build run only for a plan. Ordinary explanations and trivial edits skip this workflow.

## Guidance map

| When | Read |
|---|---|
| Writing, revising or validating task artifacts, or executing an approved plan | rule `plan-task-schema` |
| A direct planning request with sufficient supplied context and no Workspace Git readiness | `{CURSOR}/skills/discovery/workspace-git-readiness.md` |

## Lifecycle boundaries

- Discovery prompt: returns the prompt in chat; runs no discovery and creates no artifacts.
- Discovery: never starts planning or Build itself; when a plan follows, it ends at a user review.
- Planning: consequential gaps return to discovery; creating a plan never starts Build.
- Build: the parent is Lead; Build never restarts discovery or planning.

Planning starts only after the user's explicit choice at discovery's review
checkpoint, even for research-and-plan requests; silence is not a choice. A direct
planning request with sufficient supplied context skips discovery; if Workspace Git
readiness is missing, run only `workspace-git-readiness.md`. Read-only artifact
review and approved-plan resume never fetch or change checkouts. Build runs only
when requested.

## Delegation

Delegate a bounded assignment when it can return a materially smaller, assessable
result; keep small or rapidly evolving coupled work in the parent. File counts and
token thresholds are not triggers. Each lifecycle skill owns its own dispatch, and
these principles grant no role additional permissions.

- Pass compact requirements, decisions, source identities, boundaries and guidance
  explicitly; never rely on chat inheritance.
- Check consequential evidence and integration boundaries before keeping a
  conclusion. Keep accepted decisions, evidence links and precise unknowns in
  existing artifacts, not raw worker trails.
- Resume the same worker for the same problem while its inputs still apply; pass
  the changes and require a focused delta naming superseded conclusions and
  affected consumers/checks. Use a fresh worker only for an obsolete assignment,
  an unavailable worker or a deliberately independent assessment, after confirming
  an uncertain worker has stopped. Do not preload earlier rationale and call the
  result independent.
- Before a context handoff, record accepted conclusions, open questions,
  provisional work and evidence freshness in existing artifacts; rebuild state from
  artifacts and sources afterwards. During Build the Lead ledger is authoritative.
- If delegation is unavailable, say so. The parent may do bounded work within its
  own permissions, never past an approval or stop boundary.

## Domain map

Select one Agent per task by the paths it owns and its behavior. A path belongs to
the deepest of `{SQL}`, `{DOTNET}` and `{CLIENT}` that holds it; several roles can
share one repository. When two roles share one folder, a path in it goes by kind:
.NET source and project files to `{DOTNET}`, client source and its workspace
configuration to `{CLIENT}`, `*.sql` files and schema projects to `{SQL}`. Code of
an unconfigured role goes to the agent whose role folder holds it (EF Core
migrations inside `{DOTNET}`, for example); if none does, the role must be
configured before that work is planned. Domain agent files are references during
discovery/planning, not roles for the parent to assume.

| Agent | Owns | Instructions |
|---|---|---|
| `implementation-sql-agent` | `{SQL}` | `{CURSOR}/agents/implementation-sql-agent.md` |
| `implementation-dotnet-agent` | `{DOTNET}` | `{CURSOR}/agents/implementation-dotnet-agent.md` |
| `implementation-client-agent` | `{CLIENT}`: apps, libs and supporting configuration | `{CURSOR}/agents/implementation-client-agent.md` |
| `generalPurpose` | Tooling and other files outside `{SQL}`, `{DOTNET}` and `{CLIENT}`, such as a separate `{TILT}`; never files inside them | None; uses `{CURSOR}/skills/implement-plan/implementation-contract.md` directly and selects extra guidance by frontmatter description |
| `orchestrator` | The final end-to-end verification task only | None; the parent runs it and never dispatches it |

Every dispatched implementation worker follows the shared implementation contract.
The planning helper and browser verifier are not implementation Agents and use
their own contracts.

## Guidance maps

Read the procedure directly, not its shim. Read only targets whose trigger matches,
and put the selected targets and references in each task's Read first. Operational
guidance applies only when its operation or runtime is involved. `read-before-write`
and `scope-creep-gate` apply at every stage.

## Planning artifact layout

New runs use `{ARTIFACTS}/planning/<plan-slug>/`, with a descriptive lowercase
kebab-case slug recorded in the plan. Reuse the slug for the same run; use a
distinct slug for unrelated work or a new run that would overwrite an approved
artifact set.

```text
planning/<plan-slug>/
  discovery/
    discovery.md              handoff, includes Workspace Git readiness
    user-flows.md             required flow handoff with stable UF IDs
    <topic>.md                only when a focused topic needs its own evidence
  <plan-slug>.plan.md         the plan
  tasks/
    01-task-<plan-slug>.md
    ...
    NN-task-<plan-slug>.md    final end-to-end verification
  verification/               final-verification evidence per attempt, then per UF ID
  execution-state.md          mutable Lead-owned execution ledger
```

`<plan-slug>.plan.md` is the plan on every host. Its YAML frontmatter holds `name`,
`overview` and `todos`: one per task in execution order, each with an `id` and a
`content` line. Task status lives in the execution ledger; a `status` field in an
older plan is ignored. The body holds global Decisions, the Escalation boundary and
Planning artifacts (the portable run root and discovery/flow handoffs). Named
workstream groups list their task ids and numbered-file links, followed by the final
integration gate; they never imply dispatch barriers. It does not duplicate task
bodies.

Each numbered file owns one task's executable contract and detail. Number files in
plan order from 01 with at least two digits. Task artifacts link relevant
discovery files and headings with relative links. Additional evidence files use
descriptive topic names, not agent ids or dates. New plans materialize supplied
discovery context here even when no research is needed. Honor explicit read-only
requests; do not present an uncreated artifact set as an executable plan.

Until Build starts, revise the plan, task and discovery files as needed and tell the
user what changed. From the start of Build until it ends, those files are the approved
artifact set and are frozen: workers never edit them, the Lead records progress and
decisions in `execution-state.md`, and a change means stopping Build and revising.

Paths and links:

- The plan, task and discovery artifacts keep `{CURSOR}`, `{WORKSPACE}`,
  `{ARTIFACTS}` and role tokens, never machine-absolute paths. Source references
  use a tokenized repository root and ref.
- Plan links to task and discovery files are relative to the run root. No
  `#fragment`; wrap paths containing spaces in angle brackets; give each link a
  readable purpose label and keep the todo id as separate metadata. Each link must
  open an existing file.

## User flows and Workspace Git readiness

The discovery skill owns `discovery/user-flows.md`, its flow template, and Workspace
Git readiness (freshness choice and feature-branch map). Planning maps every required
UF ID to implementation tasks and exact final verification steps through the existing
Discovery/Done when/Verification fields, and carries the branch map into Decisions;
Build enforces the map before dispatch. Uncovered flows block readiness; technical
checks alone do not cover a flow. A source/base change after research invalidates
affected discovery, flows and contracts for reviewed revalidation; never silently
refresh frozen evidence.
